  <KeyTakeaways
    items={[
      'MC1R, the receptor that sets red hair and fair skin, is also active in the nervous system — so its common loss-of-function "red-hair" variants track with measurable differences in pain and anaesthesia.',
      'In a controlled study, redheaded women needed about 19% more of the inhaled anaesthetic desflurane than dark-haired women.',
      'Redheads have also been shown to be more sensitive to thermal pain and more resistant to injected lidocaine — a plausible basis for the widely reported trouble with dental freezing.',
      'Yet the same variants can mean more relief from certain opioids: a female-specific boost from kappa-opioids and an enhanced response to the morphine metabolite M6G.',
